## 4. The probability law does not see the Record offset

The Block-09 law depends only on the symmetric trace-free part of the odd
shell matrix.  The same Record content appears at both ends of the `f` pair
in (2), so it cancels from (3).  Consequently all fourteen probability
expressions, their normalization, and their second moment are exactly the
unchanged Block-09 functions of `F`.

The scalar and antisymmetric action coordinates still have zero leakage into
the probability law, while the quadrupole source identity remains

\[
 Q=-48\,M.                                             \tag{5}
\]

The probability-stage function accepts only the recognized predecessor
Record and the six addressed neighbor contents.  It has no realized-outcome
argument.  Only after the distribution is formed does the post-formation
stage receive the realized label `b` and write `r_(f,b)`.  Thus the outcome
does not enter its own probability.

## 5. The same five quantum cells generate the successor

After a Record forms at site `x`, use the five edges

```text
x+f       -> x+2f
x+e1      -> x+f+e1
x-e1      -> x+f-e1
x+e2      -> x+f+e2
x-e2      -> x+f-e2
```

where `e1,e2` span the coordinate plane perpendicular to `f`.  For every one
of the six fronts these are five pairwise disjoint nearest-neighbor edges.
Applying SWAP on each edge moves each source state to its exact required
destination.  It does not clone it.  The arbitrary prior destination quantum
states are moved backward, so the construction assumes neither a preferred
blank state nor a preloaded future quantum packet.  It does, however, require
those five destinations to be no-Record sites.  Their `M2` contents may be
arbitrary; their permanent-Record status may not.  The current probability
stencil cannot see all five statuses.

The new Record at `x` is the backward neighbor of the next target `x+f`.
Define

\[
 F'=F+{1\over2}(r_{f,a}-r_{f,b})f^T.                  \tag{6}
\]

Then the transported states satisfy, identically,

\[
 2F'f+r_{f,b}=2Ff+r_{f,a},\qquad F'n=Fn\quad(n\perp f).
                                                               \tag{7}
\]

Thus the five live quantum states do not change at all; only their positions
and their decoding relative to the newest Record change.  The primary runner
checks all `6 x 14 x 14 = 1176` front/predecessor/successor combinations,
including exact source and destination addresses, arbitrary destination
contents, and the returned backward states.

This transport is an outcome-independent post-formation instrument stage on
the collision-free registered domain.
Its effective trigger is the occurrence of the new Record event, once.  A
persistent static Record trigger would require extra one-shot memory and is
not claimed.  The probability stencil has radius one, while the subsequent
operation is a finite-depth circuit of nearest-neighbor gates; the combined
event is not advertised as one simultaneous radius-one channel.

## 6. Why every finite prefix follows

Iterating (6) gives

\[
 F_N=F_0+{1\over2}(r_{f,b_0}-r_{f,b_N})f^T,           \tag{8}
\]

because all intermediate Record terms telescope.  On a collision-free
corridor the live packet always
contains the same five physical `M2` states, so its size stays exactly five
and its positivity cannot degrade with history length.  The current Record
is always one of the 84 strictly physical code states.

The Block-09 distribution is normalized and has strict universal floors on
every physical six-neighbor shell.  Hence, for every finite history,

\[
 \sum_{b_N}P(b_1,\ldots,b_N)=P(b_1,\ldots,b_{N-1}).   \tag{9}
\]

The runner evaluates the two-step identity for all fourteen first outcomes
in all six fronts and proves the same-rule induction using (7)--(9).  It also
checks straight trails of lengths one through eight in every front: earlier
Records remain unique and permanent, every older Record points to an already
recorded successor, and exactly the newest Record points to one unrecorded
forward site.

This is a single conditional straight history.  The identities do not supply
the empty corridor: one common infinite realization needs an unbounded
Record-free strip, while a length-`N` realization needs only the corresponding
finite strip.  Interacting fronts, branching, collisions, a collision-safe
termination rule, a whole-lattice scheduling law, and seed production are
outside the quantified result.

